---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | aiPressHQ"
  description="What aiPressHQ collects, what it doesn't, and how the site's local-storage features work."
>
  <section class="legal-page" aria-labelledby="legal-title">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <span class="label">aiPressHQ / Privacy Policy</span>
      <h1 id="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated August 6, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose legal-body">
      <p>
        aiPressHQ is a news and explainer site about artificial intelligence. This page explains
        what information the site collects when you read it, what it doesn't, and how the few
        client-side features that remember anything actually work.
      </p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        There are no accounts, no mailing list, no ad network, and no analytics or tracking
        scripts on this site. The only data that gets stored lives in your own browser's local
        storage and is never sent to aiPressHQ's servers.
      </p>

      <h2>What we don't collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No sign-up, login, or account system.</li>
        <li>No forms, comments, or mailing list sign-ups.</li>
        <li>No advertising, ad networks, or ad-targeting pixels.</li>
        <li>No analytics or behavioral tracking scripts of any kind.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What's stored in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        A few optional features use your browser's <code>localStorage</code> to remember things on
        your device between visits. None of this is transmitted to us — it stays on your device
        until you clear it.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Saved stories</strong> — the list of articles you bookmark for later.</li>
        <li><strong>Recent searches</strong> — your last few searches on this site, shown as shortcuts.</li>
        <li><strong>Theme preference</strong> — whether you last chose light or dark mode.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can clear any of this at any time by clearing your browser's site data for
        aiPressHQ, or by using the remove controls built into the saved-stories and search
        features themselves.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        aiPressHQ does not set cookies. See the <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a> for details
        on why, and on how the local-storage features above differ from cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting and infrastructure</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served from Cloudflare's network (Cloudflare Pages/Workers), with images
        delivered from Cloudflare R2 and article content sourced from Prismic, our headless
        content management system. These are backend infrastructure providers, not
        user-tracking services, and neither is configured to collect visitor data on
        aiPressHQ's behalf beyond the standard technical request logs any web host keeps for
        security and reliability (such as IP address, user agent, and request timestamp).
        Cloudflare's own handling of that data is governed by its <a
          href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Articles link out to the sources they report on — official documentation, company
        announcements, research papers, and other outlets. Once you follow a link off
        aiPressHQ, that site's own privacy practices apply, not this one.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        aiPressHQ is a general-audience news site and is not directed at children under 13. We
        do not knowingly collect personal information from children.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If what the site collects or how it's stored changes, this page will be updated and the
        date above will change accordingly.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to <a
          href="mailto:privacy@aipresshq.com">privacy@aipresshq.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
